      "text": "I've recorded the assessment as **UNKNOWN**, with no sample characterization yet, and I've asked for a human to step in.\n\n- **Why unknown:** The growth stage needs a pressure gauge, and this furnace doesn't have one. So I can't confirm the tube pressure or the atmosphere during growth.\n- **What looks fine:**\n  - Temperature followed the ramp closely and is holding at 749–751 °C, after a short overshoot to 760 °C.\n  - Heater power is steady at about 44%.\n  - Argon flow is on its 100 sccm setpoint.\n  - Oxygen dropped normally during the purge and has stayed around 5 ppm, which argues against an air leak.\n- **What stays unchecked:** A blocked exhaust would mainly show up as a pressure change, and none of the installed sensors would clearly catch it.\n- **Next step:** Someone should decide whether running without a pressure gauge is acceptable, or check the pressure another way. After that, the sample needs characterizing to answer whether the material grew."
